Adal is a tengu of [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], of the noble [[People/Qureshi|Qureshi]] family, the father of [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] and [[People/Galzu|Galzu]], and a noble of [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]. He speaks of his family's minds as their strongest asset and looks down on art made without a patron.

He knows where Anzu is hiding, having traced him through the archive Anzu visited in [[Geography/Calaria/index|Calaria]], and he reaches him by fax at the [[Sin and Tonic]]. He has talked the rest of the family out of digging too deep and kept the news from Ishta, who is not happy with Anzu. He wants Anzu to call his mother now and then so the family knows he is well, and has offered him another identity if he wants to stay hidden.

Galzu worries him more. She stormed out of the roost and has not come back. He knows nothing of the break-in at the Belvedere facility the night she vanished, though the site was near where Anzu's grandmother had been that night. If Galzu is hiding with the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]], he means to put pressure on them.
